  "description": "Shore buildings and land by the water (ARCHITECTURE decision 111): free play, 32768 x 32768 units (8 x 8 cells of 64 m), no stations, no land. setWater makes rows 0 and 1 water (two runs of 8 cells, 16 cells). A wharf (24 m, 1536 units a side) and a marina (32 m, 2048) stand on the shore: part of their square over water and part on land. A marina centred at (20480, 20480), wholly on land in rows 4 and 5, or at (20480, 2048), wholly over the water of row 0, is refused with needsShore. A wharf centred at (6144, 8192), on row 2's north edge (y 7424 to 8960: rows 1, water, and 2, land), is building 1. A house there, centred at (14336, 8192) (x 13824 to 14848, column 3), is still refused with onWater naming (1, 3), the first water cell under it. A marina centred at (22528, 8192) (x 21504 to 23552, columns 5 and 6; rows 1 and 2) is building 2; free play pays nothing. Land value with no station is the empty cell's base, 1000 cents a m2; a cell whose middle lies within 160 m (10240 units) of a water cell's middle, the water's own cells included, adds waterPremium 600: (0, 0), water, 1600; (3, 4), 2 rows (8192 units, 128 m) from row 1, 1600; (4, 4), 3 rows (12288, 192 m), 1000; (7, 7), 1000. Every value is worked out by hand.",
